From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:13:30 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Try with Claude, for designers and everyone else
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The welcome tour moves Arc in first, then "We found Claude": one Yes adds
Meridian to Claude for Mac, a step explains its restart and its Allow
question (with a little drawing of it), and "Try it with Claude" offers five
cards: a new look for a site (Boost), a Pinterest moodboard, a senior
designer's critique, tidy my tabs and what else Meridian can do. Each card
gets the page ready and opens Claude with the request typed in (and on the
clipboard); Claude restarts first when it started before Meridian was added.
The same cards are on the home page and behind ⌘T's "Try with Claude…";
without Claude, a way to get it and Ask instead.

Who uses the computer is guessed from design apps and strong developer
signs (repositories, Homebrew, coding agents): Workbench and Mission Control
show for developers only. Tests record Claude's links
(--meridian-test-claude-log) and never open Claude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
